`forEach`
 indeed. Each of the 
`async`
 callback function calls does return a promise, but you're throwing them away instead of awaiting them. Just use 
`map`
 instead, and you can await the array of promises that you'll get with 
`Promise.all`
:

```javascript
async function printFiles () {
  const files = await getFilePaths();

  await Promise.all(files.map(async (file) => {
    const contents = await fs.readFile(file, 'utf8')
    console.log(contents)
  }));
}
```

